<header><p class="st-kicker">imperial city · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Free Imperial City of Donauwörth</h1><p class="st-meta">1301 CE – 1607 CE (approx.) · capital Donauwörth</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Swabian imperial city on the Danube whose sectarian riot of 1606 and seizure by Bavaria helped set Europe on the road to the Thirty Years' War.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Donauwörth grew where the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wornitz">Wörnitz</a> meets the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a>, beside the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-cross-abbey-donauworth">Holy Cross abbey</a> and a castle. A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hohenstaufen">Hohenstaufen</a> possession, it later fell under the dukes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>, from whom it repeatedly bought back its freedom. It counted as an imperial city from about 1301, although it was pledged to Bavaria again from 1376 until 1434.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>A council of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burghers">burghers</a> governed the town, which prospered from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> trade and the road between <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-imperial-city-of-nuremberg">Nuremberg</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-imperial-city-of-augsburg">Augsburg</a>. Most citizens became Lutheran, while the Benedictine <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-cross-abbey-donauworth">Holy Cross abbey</a> kept a Catholic minority. In 1606 Protestant townspeople attacked a Catholic procession, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aulic-council">Imperial Aulic Council</a> placed the city under the imperial ban.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maximilian-i-elector-of-bavaria">Duke Maximilian</a> I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> executed the ban in 1607, occupied Donauwörth, re-Catholicised it and in 1609 annexed it. Alarmed Protestant princes formed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-union">Protestant Union</a> in 1608, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catholic-league">Catholic League</a> answered in 1609. Apart from a brief restoration of its imperial freedom from 1705 to 1714, the town has remained Bavarian ever since.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="imperial city, 1301 CE – 1607 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54 H40 M60 54 H66"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">imperial city</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Germany and Central Europe</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:85.59%;width:6.09%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1301 CE – 1607 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>imperial city</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Donauwörth</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Lutheranism, Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Swabian German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Donauwörth</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1454&amp;focus=free-imperial-city-of-donauworth" aria-label="Free Imperial City of Donauwörth on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4929 476 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Free Imperial City of Donauwörth lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5249 732L5229 694M5249 732L5279 723"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5229 694h0M5279 723h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5249 732h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5249 732h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Donauwörth. <a href="/atlas?year=1454&amp;focus=free-imperial-city-of-donauworth">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

